>>
Rule 1 (tensor input must have at least 4 dimensions)
{theta : tensor} |= ndim(theta) ≥ 4
>>
Rule 2 (tensor input must be valid for affine grid generation)
{theta : tensor} |= shape(theta, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(theta, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(theta, 2) > 0 ∧ shape(theta, 3) > 0
>>
Rule 3 (integer parameters should be positive)
{N : int, C : int, H : int, W : int} |= N > 0 ∧ C > 0 ∧ H > 0 ∧ W > 0
>>
Rule 4 (tensor input must match the expected shape for affine grid generation)
{theta : tensor} |= shape(theta, 0) = N ∧ shape(theta, 1) = C ∧ shape(theta, 2) = H ∧ shape(theta, 3) = W
>>
Rule 6 (tensor input must be compatible with shape)
{theta : tensor} |= ndim(theta) ≥ 4 ∧ shape(theta, 0) = N ∧ shape(theta, 1) = C ∧ shape(theta, 2) = H ∧ shape(theta, 3) = W
